xmrswap under a REAL Monero reorganisation (MT-B11): regtest monerod and monero-wallet-rpc, and the DERO simulator
================================================================================================================
Run 2026-09-11 from 18:47 AEST: tools/simhtlc -regtest -paths reorg-before,reorg-after, built from the working
tree. The raw driver output follows this header; machine paths are written <tmp>, <repo> and <user>.

What is real, and what the reorganisation is
- Monero: monerod 0.18.5.1-release, nettype fakechain, http://127.0.0.1:28081, and two monero-wallet-rpc 0.18.5.1
  (alice http://127.0.0.1:28083, bob http://127.0.0.1:28084), in WSL2, started per tools/regtest/README.md and not
  restarted. Every Monero call the companions made went to them.
- The reorganisation is made on that monerod through its own RPC. pop_blocks takes the block holding alice's lock,
  and every block after it, off the chain; monerod puts their transactions back in its pool, and flush_txpool then
  removes the lock from the pool so that no branch can include it again. generateblocks mines a longer branch at
  the same heights. The block hash at the lock's height is read before and after: a different block is there. The
  wallets and the companions see what a reorganisation is to them: blocks at heights they had already scanned have
  been replaced, and a transaction they had seen confirmed is on no chain. It is not a competing miner's branch
  arriving over p2p (the regtest monerod has no peers). The two differ in how the node comes to change chains, not
  in what the wallets see once it has.
- DERO: the local simulator (daemon 127.0.0.1:20000, wallets 127.0.0.1:30006 bob and 127.0.0.1:30007 alice), not
  testnet or mainnet. A DERO-side reorganisation CANNOT be produced on it: the simulator is one node mining its own
  chain, with no second chain to change to and no call that takes blocks off. The companions' handling of a DERO
  reorganisation (Invariant 9 and U3: a Claim is acted on only once it is at stable depth, and a Claim that vanishes
  sends each side back) has run only against the in-memory fake chain (TestTakerWatchesHerClaimUntilStable, the
  crash fuzz), never against a real DERO chain.
- Proofs: the pinned proof-xmr release build, through wsl.exe.
- Driver policy, not the companion's defaults: t1 = lock + 48 DERO blocks, t2 = t1 + 8, G = 4, bob's depth 10
  Monero confirmations (the companion's default is 20), one regtest block mined per driver round, SweepWaits at the
  companion's default of 240 passes.

Command (from <repo>/tools, built to simhtlc_reorg.exe):
  simhtlc -regtest -paths reorg-before,reorg-after -prover "wsl.exe -e <path to the pinned proof-xmr release build>"
          -state-dir <tmp>/e2estate_reorg
  (every other flag at its default: -daemon 127.0.0.1:20000 -bob 127.0.0.1:30006 -alice 127.0.0.1:30007
   -monero-alice http://127.0.0.1:28083 -monero-bob http://127.0.0.1:28084 -monerod http://127.0.0.1:28081)
Pre-run check (first line of the raw output): no other simhtlc or xmrswap process, no transfer on 30006 or 30007
since DERO height 911, and an empty monerod pool.

